# Living documentation

Per-entry files, per the doqs convention — not single accumulating documents.

| Location | Purpose | Update trigger |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `docs/dev-log/YYYY-MM-DD_topic.md` | What was done, chronologically | A working session worth recording |
| `docs/decisions/YYYY-MM-DD_topic.md` | ADRs | A non-trivial technical choice |
| `docs/mistakes/YYYY-MM-DD_topic.md` | Errors and prevention rules | After a mistake or failed approach |
| `docs/prompts-log/YYYY-MM.md` | AI interaction log | Ongoing |
| `.claude/skills/project-patterns/SKILL.md` | Reusable project patterns | A pattern proves out or changes |

Templates are in `doqs/templates/`. Each folder has a `README.md` index — **update it when adding a
file**, or the entry becomes invisible.

`docs/architecture.md` is a short overview and pointer to `doqs/docs/architecture.md`. Component
detail belongs next to its code, in that module's `README.md`.
